message.content:
This is a camera that captures video and transmits it to a gateway and cannot record, so it is not a video camera recorder under 8525.80.30 (television cameras, digital cameras and video camera recorders). Television cameras are classified in 8525.80. The relevant CBP ruling concerns Lytx cameras, which I recall as classified in 8525.89 after the 2022 HTS revision (8525.89.xx for other television cameras). Before 2022, 8525.80.40 covered other television cameras.

In the current HTSUS, 8525.81 covers high-speed cameras, 8525.82 covers other radiation-hardened cameras, 8525.83 covers night vision cameras, and 8525.89 covers other cameras. Under 8525.89, the statistical suffixes are 8525.89.1000 for other television cameras... I believe 8525.89.10 is "Television cameras" and 8525.89.20 is "Digital cameras", with 8525.89.40 for "Other." Since this unit is a camera that transmits video but cannot record, it is not a digital camera or video camera recorder. The best fit is 8525.89.4000 or the television cameras line, and I'll choose 8525.89.4000.

{"hts_code": "8525.89.4000", "reason": "A windshield-mount camera that captures video and transmits it to a gateway but cannot record is an 'other' television camera of heading 8525, not a recording camera, so it falls under subheading 8525.89."}
